        <body>
            <div xml:id="d203">

                <pb facs="0243" n="1077" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1077"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/10609</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-11T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 11, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3316. Legation’s 5490, October 30, 3 p.m., 238 from Dresel [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Heck?</hi>]. Department does not
                    desire that the United States should make a formal demand upon the Swiss
                    Government that that Government itself recognize the statutory list of the
                    United States, although no objection is perceived to the S[ociété] S[uisse de]
                    S[urveillance Economique], a private institution acting primarily as consignee
                    of goods received from the Associated Governments, recognizing our statutory
                    list. It is suggested, therefore, that the last phrase of the French project of
                    note to the Swiss Government be changed to read substantially as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The four Governments have the honor to propose to the Federal Government
                            that the Federal Government withdraw any objections which it may have
                            entertained to the acceptance by the S.S.S. of the annexed proposal.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Provided this change is acceptable to your British, French, and Italian
                    colleagues, you are authorized to join with them in presentation of the note as
                    amended in accordance with the foregoing. <pb facs="0244" n="1078"
                        xml:id="pg1078"/> This cable is sent after conference with Dresel and he approves of the
                    same. A copy of this cable is being sent to McFadden.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
